{
 "note": "Mutants of the test maps of the Map Maker's 'With other players' (src/ants_server/test_maps.cpp, test_maps_http.cpp and their headers; the refusals, the findings, the address and the checking window that the door shares with the real submissions door are upload_common.cpp, whose mutants are tests/data/submissions_mutants.json) for tools/mutate.py (docs/WORKFLOW.md, 'Mutation checks'). Run from the checkout with a configured build folder: python3 tools/mutate.py tests/data/test_maps_mutants.json --keep-going --jobs 1 --timeout 900. Every mutant must be caught by test_test_maps: each breaks one rule of docs/MAP_SUBMISSIONS.md ('Test maps'): the canonical file, the limits (an hour for an address and for all, the checking window and its time, the count, the held bytes, the maps of one address, what a room has, six hours), the one route and its method, the body limit, the folder's modes and what the start wipes, the name that is made of a typed one, the size limit of a room. Not listed on purpose: a '/' allowed by the name's first filter (clean_map_name refuses it behind it, so no test can see the mutant: a second lock), the draw of an id that is held already (it is random, so no test can make it happen: a second lock against a write over a held file), the allowance of nginx (tests/scripts/test_nginx_test_maps.py holds the text and runs the blocks), and the page (tests/data/rematch_mutants.json). The room that keeps no replay on a test map has two locks that each make the other equivalent (RoomManager::create_room and Room::replay_begin): test_room_records_a_test_match breaks the name test they share (test_server S3.163b).",
 "defaults": {
  "build": "test_test_maps",
  "test": "./build/tests/test_server/test_test_maps"
 },
